From c3b75bbeb207dce4d2bcce93d2f09e8036c08971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:23:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: dspark draft, host half (config, names,
 rank plan, float64 reference, twins, budget, refusals)

Adds the base model's dspark speculative-decoding draft as host-testable code and a design (docs/dspark-plan.md in the recipe):
dspark_config (parse the pack's dspark/config.json, admit against the target, byte arithmetic, MoE window cost model),
dspark_names (the 97 tensors of the header), dspark_load (per-rank plan over load.Catalog; mxfp8 codes and ue8m0 scales cut
as the target's heads and dense MLP, no Gemma fold), dspark_ref (float64 mxfp8 decode, taps, context state, 5-layer
sliding-window block, Markov chain, confidence, every unverified semantic a named switch), dspark_twin (K/V ring, two-rank
block, per-rank candidate gather, each with planted mutants), budget.Terms.draft / withDraft / Refusal.draft, and native's
takes_drafter = false with the draft-specific --drafter refusal. Step test-minimax-dspark (also under test-cuda-host).
No kernels, no engine integration, no GPU. The semantics are UNVERIFIED: the upstream modeling code was unavailable.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
